            <p>Decorticate Posturing. The image shows a man with flexed arms&#x000a0;and clenched fists held across the chest, alongside extended and internally rotated lower limbs. This posture indicates a lesion above the red nucleus with preserved rubrospinal tract function mediating upper limb flexion and unopposed vestibulospinal tract activity causing lower limb extension. Contributed by Katherine Humphreys</p>
